This directory is a copy of libdcerpc, which lives in the libsmb2
repository (https://github.com/sahlberg/libsmb2, directory libdcerpc/).
It was taken from commit f55a0e286adb7b4c7cacf0b132bb9f9344171ad5.

ksmbd-tools uses the coders for srvsvc, wkssvc, lsarpc, samr and dssetup
and the server runtime, <dcerpc/server.h>, which does BIND, fragments
and NDR32/NDR64 in either byte order on the bytes mountd gets from the
kernel. It is built the way libsmb2 builds it with --without-libsmb2
(HAVE_LIBSMB2 undefined): coders and server runtime only, no transport,
no client side. It is linked statically into ksmbd.tools and nothing
from it is installed.

Copied unchanged from libsmb2/libdcerpc/:

  dcerpc.c dcerpc-dtyp.c dcerpc-epm.c dcerpc-server.c dcerpc-unicode.c
  dcerpc-private.h include/dcerpc/*.h idlcomp.py <iface>/<iface>.idl
  COPYING README

The coders are generated from the IDL at build time by idlcomp.py, so
python3 is needed to build. All eight interfaces are kept, also winreg,
netlogon and epm which ksmbd-tools does not serve, because
dcerpc_create_context() registers every coder.

Left out: dcerpcd/, utils/, examples/, tests/, dcerpc-examples/,
packaging/, libdcerpc.syms, schannel.c (the Netlogon secure channel,
used only by the client side) and libdcerpc's own build files, which
meson.build, include/dcerpc/meson.build and Makefile.am here replace.

To update, copy the files listed above from a newer libsmb2 and change
the commit at the top. Fixes belong upstream in libsmb2, not here.
